# Copy to .env (or `source` it / set these in your shell) to point this checkout
# at a differently-located data_clean/ instead of the default `./data_clean/`
# (e.g. a shared network folder). The target must be a FLAT folder containing
# layer1_crowns.csv, layer1_tiles_disjoint.csv, layer2_nodes.csv, layer2_panel.csv,
# layer2_edges.csv, and Eg9PP_Phenotypes.csv directly — the same flat shape
# scripts/download_assets.py produces by default. See src/oil_palm/config.py
# for exactly what this does and does not affect (weights are NOT independently
# overridable this way — see that file's docstring).

SAWITGUARD_DATA_ROOT=/path/to/a/flat/data_clean/folder
